WEBVTT

NOTE Module: Databases

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:11.835
In Module 8, we explore database design and PostgreSQL engineering. We study normalization, B-Tree indexes, transaction isolation levels, and ACID guarantees.

2
00:00:11.835 --> 00:00:22.579
Atomic database transactions guarantee that related operations succeed together. If any statement fails, the transaction rolls back, preserving database integrity.

3
00:00:22.579 --> 00:00:32.196
A common pitfall is forgetting to index foreign keys. Without indexes, join queries trigger full table scans that degrade performance as data scales.

4
00:00:32.196 --> 00:00:41.614
Demonstrate relational schema design, query optimization, and transaction safety in our practical labs to qualify your database competency.
